%% Tenant storage upload, validation, namespace, and evidence linkage
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as Customer or admin
    participant Web as Web/BFF
    participant API as Storage API
    participant Guard as Tenant auth and policy
    participant Validate as Upload validator
    participant Store as Object storage strategy
    participant Scan as Malware/quarantine path
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Feature as Warranty/content feature

    User->>Web: Select file for tenant feature
    Web->>API: Request upload or presigned PUT
    API->>Guard: Resolve tenant, actor, feature, and ownership
    Guard->>Validate: Check size, type, filename, and purpose
    Validate-->>API: Validated upload contract
    API->>Store: Generate tenant-scoped object key
    Store-->>API: Presigned upload URL and safe public metadata
    API-->>Web: Presigned upload URL and safe public metadata
    Web->>Store: Upload bytes directly to object storage
    Store->>Scan: Apply malware/quarantine policy
    Scan-->>Store: Clean, pending, or quarantined result

    alt Accepted clean evidence
        Web->>API: Confirm upload metadata
        API->>DB: Persist object reference in tenant record
        API->>Feature: Attach evidence to warranty/content entity
        Feature->>DB: Save tenant-local evidence link
    else Quarantined or rejected
        Store-->>API: Safe failure state
        API-->>Web: Safe failure state
        API->>DB: Persist sanitized failure/evidence state when required
    end

    Note over Store,DB: Object key namespace includes the trusted organization identity; browser-supplied cross-tenant keys are rejected.
    Note over Validate,Scan: File acceptance is not the same as malware-clean evidence until the scan/quarantine policy completes.
